From 888b820f7be19e6d0ed0bd7418a2a25a3c099c13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:54:29 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 60/62] Frame interpolation: a split screen's two views

Each draw now carries the view of a split frame it belongs to (before the
left marker, between the markers, after the compose). Draws pair only within
their view, each view has its own camera motion for the blend and the
own-motion guard, and the cut limits apply to every view. The compose moves
each view's middle into its half instead of scaling it by a pixel, so a
replay draws each view's draws straight into its half (viewport moved, scissor
cut at the half) and clears the dark line before what lies over both. A frame
that starts or ends the split is a cut.

Checked on Dissidia 012 (Windows, RX 9070 XT): a split frame drawn again from
its recording matches the frame (no pixel off by more than 8/255), 60 of 60
fps through a fight, and a one-view battle unchanged (replay checks exact).
New test: split_views. Not checked: the Steam Deck.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
